maps.summary:
Wuying AgentBay (无影 AgentBay) is Alibaba Cloud's hosted sandbox service for agents. It has four environments: Browser Use (image browser_latest), Computer Use (linux_latest, windows_latest), Code Space (code_latest) and Mobile Use (mobile_latest). Access is through SDKs (Python, TypeScript, Go, Java; Apache-2.0) or an MCP server, authenticated with an API key.

The browser sandbox has the features we would want:
- a CDP WebSocket endpoint for Playwright or Puppeteer;
- persistent browser "contexts" that keep cookies and local storage between sessions;
- a resource_url that lets a person watch or take over the session live;
- a "call-for-user" takeover protocol for login, payment and CAPTCHA steps;
- automatic CAPTCHA solving, slider-type only;
- stealth and fingerprint options;
- custom, Wuying-provided or managed proxies, and SOCKS5 egress redirection;
- session replay (rrweb), screenshots and file upload/download.

Three facts matter most for us:
1. The CDP endpoint is not available on the free Basic plan. It needs at least Pro: CNY 999/month on the domestic site, USD 149/month on the international site. The Session Link (GetLink) feature also needs enterprise real-name verification, and as of Oct 2025 it was whitelist-only.
2. No Tokyo or Japan region is documented anywhere. Domestic-site API keys work with mainland regions (Hangzhou per SDK v0.22; older help pages say the Shanghai endpoint). International keys work with Singapore (ap-southeast-1) and Virginia (us-east-1). Keys cannot be used across regions.
3. Pay-as-you-go pricing is per second. Domestic: CPU CNY 0.12/core/hour and memory CNY 0.05/GB/hour (page last modified 2026-06-24). International: USD 0.027/core/hour and USD 0.0113/GB/hour (page "Updated: Jun 25"). Idle running sessions are billed.

Limits:
- Concurrency: Basic 10, Pro and Ultra 200. Ultra can add more at CNY 10 or USD 1.5 per concurrent session per month.
- Session lifetime: up to 1000 minutes per run, hibernation up to 72 hours. SDK defaults are a 5-minute idle timeout (backend minimum 3) and a 30-minute maximum runtime.

The product launched at WAIC on 2025-07-31 after about three months of internal testing. The current billing model started 2025-10-28. No GA or preview label was found. No AgentBay SLA document was found; the only SLA mention is that Premium bandwidth comes with one. Several sub-features are labelled Beta, and the docs contradict each other in several places.

options.when_best:
Best when:
- most browsing is of foreign or global sites, docs, SaaS and research, which tolerate a Tokyo datacenter IP;
- we want egress, cost and data control in our own hands, and we have to build the WBS 2.7 egress proxy anyway;
- scale runs from tens to a few thousand daily users, where the AgentBay plan floor and region problem make buying worse;
- the team can spend about 1.5 person-months on phase 1 and another 1.5 on live view and takeover.

Start with the same-container design, sized at 1 vCPU / 4 GiB and measured before choosing 2 vCPU / 4 GiB. Move to variant (a), a sidecar container, if Chromium security rebuilds across five agent images become painful. Consider variant (b), an on-demand pod, only if measurements show browsing is well under half of agent running time at scale.

Not the right tool for:
- logged-in Chinese consumer sites (Taobao, WeChat, banks, posting on Xiaohongshu): use the user's own computer through the desktop app (WBS 14.4);
- out-of-the-box CAPTCHA solving, residential or mainland IPs and stealth: for those, a mainland browser pool (AgentRun or AgentBay) could later plug into the same CDP slot.

Get legal advice on the cross-border streaming question before launch.

This is the right choice now: launch with about 10 test users growing toward 100–1000 DAU, a tight budget, and mostly public-web tasks. Typical tasks are research, reading docs, filling forms on public sites, and checking pages the agent built.

Build it in this order:
1. Stage A: egress proxy plus the in-sandbox browser, about 34.5 person-days.
2. Stage B: live view, takeover and vault fill, about 22 person-days.

Turn on Tier 3 (AgentBay domestic, about 10 person-days plus ¥999/month) only when at least one of these holds:
- a meaningful share of tasks, say more than 20% [A], fail on Chinese sites because of the Japan IP or risk controls;
- users without a Mac need logged-in mainland sites;
- revenue covers the fixed fee.

Revisit the size choice after the Phase 0 measurement. If Chromium needs 2C/4G and usage passes about 500 DAU, an on-demand ACS browser pool (about ¥3.2 per DAU per month) or AgentBay becomes cheaper than permanently larger sandboxes.

Choose a mostly-bought design (all AgentBay) only if three things change together:
- we drop the requirement that sandbox egress goes only through our policy;
- most target sites are Chinese and need a mainland IP;
- live view must ship in days rather than weeks.

checks.claim:
Cost comparisons price our Tokyo pods at the ACS general-purpose rate (¥0.0886/vCPU·h, ¥0.0443/GiB·h):
- the alternatives survey's '+1C2G ≈ ¥0.177/h, +2C4G ≈ ¥0.354/h in Tokyo';
- the AgentBay option's 'build ourselves = ¥0.354/h, so AgentBay domestic costs ~24% more per hour' and its ¥611 (100 DAU) / ¥6,113 (1000 DAU) comparison.

Image growth estimates for the browser layer:
- self: about 0.45–0.6 GB per template;
- hybrid: about 415 MB, with Claude going from 695 MB to about 1.1 GB;
- agents survey: Chromium adds about 230–324 MB.

OpenClaw 2026.10.3:
- its ACP bridge rejects per-session mcpServers;
- the browser plugin is enabledByDefault, built on playwright-core 1.63.0;
- managed Chrome ignores HTTP(S)_PROXY;
- its docs say complete egress isolation needs a policy-enforcing proxy;
- it supports attachOnly.

Self option cost arithmetic:
- light case: ¥7.39 per DAU, 100 DAU ≈ ¥795, 1000 DAU ≈ ¥8,066;
- 1 vCPU / 4 GiB: ¥426 and ¥4,370;
- variant (b): ¥302 and ¥3,318;
- heavy case: ¥1,667 / ¥16,900, ¥928 / ¥9,500, ¥990 / ¥10,300;
- break-evens: 100% and 50%.

AgentBay option cost arithmetic:
- ¥0.44/h and $0.0992/h;
- ¥1,075 / ¥1,758 / ¥8,589 for 10 / 100 / 1000 DAU;
- $166 / $320 / $1,860;
- sensitivity runs: ¥3,529 and ¥17,559 (Ultra + 88 extra sessions);
- peak concurrency about 14 and about 144;
- plan fee is 93% of the bill at 10 DAU.

Hybrid option cost arithmetic:
- Tier 1: ¥815 / ¥8,387 (lean ¥261 / ¥2,843);
- Tier 3: ¥1,056 / ¥1,571;
- totals: ¥1,871 / ¥9,958;
- all-AgentBay: ¥1,571 / ¥6,719;
- break-even about 600 DAU;
- browser pool: ¥3,203;
- Codex/Pi: ¥9.24 per DAU;
- abandoned takeover: ¥11.8.
